  "note_asuswrt": "The linux-4.19 tree defines REG_A6XX_PDC_GPU_* with different absolute values (0x00021140 etc.) because its rnndb generation predates the PDC address rebase. Only the v6.1.11+ generation (quard_star_611, acrn) carries the modern 0x1140/0x1540 block; the verifier uses the quard_star table as the canonical base and compares PDC defines only among modern-generation sources. The RSCC block lives in the separate a6xx_gmu.xml.h in all three trees and all three agree. See verify-adreno-pdc-offsets.py.",
